            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Usually a dry deck. Lubricate with the silicone and amount your manual specifies before touching the tension bolts. If it still slips under a firm foot plant, tighten both rear bolts equally a quarter turn at a time, stopping as soon as the slip goes. A belt that slips after both is worn.",
          },
